{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_security_model_shared_secret_identity", "label": "Identity is a shared secret", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 5-18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A workspace has one 32-byte secret and possession of it is membership. There is no per-peer identity and no signing key, so `from` in an envelope is a claim rather than an assertion. Deliberate simplification: per-peer keypairs and signed envelopes would be a protocol change, not a configuration change."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_workspace_secret", "label": "32-byte workspace secret", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 7, 38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "32 random bytes from crypto.randomBytes, printed as ddk1_<base64url>. Holding it is membership, so it is treated like a password."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_peer_impersonation", "label": "Threat: any member can impersonate any member", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted consequence of the shared-secret identity: nothing binds a peer name to a key."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_member_reads_all_mail", "label": "Threat: any member reads every message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One key decrypts every inbox in the workspace, including mail addressed to other peers."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_member_deletes_all_mail", "label": "Threat: any member deletes every message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Authorisation over the store belongs to the transport, not to dead-drop, so dead-drop cannot bound delete."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_revocation_by_rotation", "label": "Revocation only by rotating the secret", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Removing a peer means rotating the secret for everybody; nothing else revokes access."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_per_peer_keypairs", "label": "Per-peer keypairs and signed envelopes (not built)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What would be needed for send-but-not-read peers or an audit trail surviving a malicious member. Explicitly out of scope for the shipping protocol."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_adr_0007", "label": "ADR 0007: per-peer key wrapping", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposes making the shared secret an enrollment token and wrapping a per-era data key to each peer's X25519 public key, so admitting a peer stops handing over the key to everything already written and removing one stops forcing a workspace-wide re-key. Proposed, not implemented."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_hostile_storage", "label": "Transport treated as hostile storage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 20-22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A GitHub repository, synced folder or S3 bucket may be readable by people outside the workspace, so nothing confidential may rely on store access control."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_encrypted_envelope", "label": "Whole envelope encrypted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 24", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Payload, channel, from, to, headers, correlation ids and content type all sit inside AES-256-GCM ciphertext."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_authenticated_preamble", "label": "Frame preamble: authenticated, not encrypted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 26, 40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frame magic, flags byte and key id stay in clear text but are the AEAD additional authenticated data, so tampering fails decryption."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_metadata_leak", "label": "Documented leak: unprotected metadata", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 28-34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Object keys, message sizes/counts/timing, and which peers exist and when they are active are visible to anyone who can read the store."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_object_key_layout", "label": "Cleartext object key layout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ws/<workspace>/inbox/<peer>/<messageId>.ddf exposes workspace names, peer names and broadcast channel names in clear text."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_traffic_analysis", "label": "Leak: sizes, counts and timing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Traffic analysis is unmitigated; no padding or cover traffic exists."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_peer_visibility", "label": "Leak: peer existence and activity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Presence is inferable from the store without any key."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_readable_keys_tradeoff", "label": "Readable keys are on purpose", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When the transport is a git repo or a folder a human has to operate, being able to look at it and understand it is worth more than the metadata it costs. If that trade is wrong, use a transport with a private backing store."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_hkdf", "label": "HKDF-SHA256 key derivation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Salt is the workspace name, info is dead-drop/v1/workspace-aead. Salting by name means the same secret in two differently-named workspaces yields unrelated keys, so a frame cannot be replayed across workspaces."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_aes_256_gcm", "label": "AES-256-GCM with per-frame random IV", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fresh random 96-bit IV per frame; the frame preamble is the additional authenticated data."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_key_id", "label": "Key id (8 hex of SHA-256)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not secret; it exists only so a receiver can pick the right key during a rotation."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_key_rotation", "label": "Two-stage key rotation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 43-52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frames name the key they were sealed with, so both keys can be accepted at once. Add the new secret second everywhere, then swap the order, then drop the old after the longest plausible in-flight TTL. Skipping the accept-both step breaks every peer not yet updated."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_ddrop_keygen", "label": "ddrop keygen", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 47", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_security_model_secret_placement", "label": "Where secrets live", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 54-59", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four negative rules: not in the config file, not in application processes, not in logs, not in printed git remote urls."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_env_expansion", "label": "${env:NAME} config expansion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ddrop init writes \"${env:DEADDROP_SECRET}\" and the parser expands it at load time, so the real value stays in a secret manager or the shell environment."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_runtime_holds_credentials", "label": "Credentials stay in the runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applications talk to the runtime over a local socket; transport credentials and workspace secrets never enter application processes."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_log_redaction", "label": "Logger redaction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redacts by field name (token, secret, authorization) and by pattern (ddk1_, ghp_, glpat-, AWS key ids, Slack tokens), including inside message text and nested objects."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_url_credential_stripping", "label": "Inline credential stripping from git urls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 59", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Credentials embedded in a remote url are stripped before any error reaches a log."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_control_plane_socket", "label": "Control plane on a 0600 Unix socket", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 61-65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never localhost TCP: a TCP port is reachable by every process on the machine, every container sharing the network namespace, and sometimes from outside, while a socket file is governed by filesystem permissions. Anything that can talk to the control plane can publish, call any peer and read runtime state, so it is the door to the whole workspace."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_exposures", "label": "Exposures and workspace-wide reach", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 67-73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ddrop expose makes a local server reachable by every peer; there is no per-request authentication beyond workspace membership."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_allow_peers", "label": "allowPeers is organisational, not a boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Peer names are self-asserted under the shared-secret identity, so restricting an exposure to named peers is an organisational control only."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_path_traversal_defense", "label": "Static exposure traversal rejection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every path resolves inside the configured root; percent-encoded .., absolute paths and null bytes are handled."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_proxy_header_hygiene", "label": "Proxy hop-by-hop stripping and no redirect following", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_security_model_dos_limits", "label": "Denial-of-service bounds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 75-88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The transport is shared and a peer can be malicious or broken, so every accepted size is bounded: 64 MiB decoded and decompressed frames, 64 MiB / 256 chunk groups, 32 MiB HTTP bodies, 1 MiB control-plane bodies, 10 000 dedupe entries for an hour."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_gzip_bomb", "label": "Gzip bomb fails as PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decompressed size is enforced by zlib rather than discovered by exhausting memory."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_undecodable_object_deletion", "label": "Undecodable objects are deleted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prevents a poison object being re-read forever."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_inbox_reaping", "label": "Reaping another peer's mail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 90-96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a recipient empties its own inbox, so mail for a peer that never returns is storage nothing reclaims. Peers delete mail older than inboxOrphanMs with no presence beacon (or a beacon older than the window). This grants no new privilege, since every member could already read and delete any inbox; what changes is that correct peers now delete data they did not author, so the risk to weigh is accidental loss. Deciding costs a listing only: age is read from the message id in the key, nothing is downloaded or decrypted, and a real TTL is unreadable from outside."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_inbox_orphan_ms", "label": "inboxOrphanMs setting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 92, 96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "7 days by default; 0 disables reaping. A peer offline longer than the window loses its mail."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_presence_beacon", "label": "Presence beacon", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The liveness signal that protects an inbox from reaping."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_adr_0006", "label": "ADR 0006: reaping orphaned inboxes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_security_model_replay_defense", "label": "Replay defence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 98-102", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unique message ids plus a dedupe store that persists across restarts drop a replayed frame. Requests are stamped with a TTL equal to their timeout, so a captured request cannot be usefully replayed after expiry. A member replaying their own traffic inside the TTL is not defended, because they could simply send the message again."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_dedupe_store", "label": "DedupeStore", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 86, 100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounded at 10 000 entries for one hour and persisted, so it serves both DoS bounding and replay defence."}, {"id": "docs_security_model_message_ttl", "label": "Message and request TTL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_security_model_private_reporting", "label": "Private security reporting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "lines 104-106", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Issues go to the repository owner privately rather than the public tracker."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_security_model_shared_secret_identity", "target": "docs_security_model_workspace_secret", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/security-model.md", "source_location": "line 7", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_security_model_shared_secret_identity", "target": "